# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/graphify/ is gitignored.
#
#   git clone --depth 1 --branch <ref> <url> sources/graphify
#   git -C sources/graphify checkout <commit>
#
# First corpus: graphify's own source, so the KB can answer "how does graphify
# work?" (esp. whether add/write is exposed via MCP or the python API) from the
# graph instead of guessing.
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the Graphify version the locked uv project installs.
# Otherwise the corpus answers questions about code we are not running. That is
# not hypothetical: until 2026-07-23 this sat at e32c9f43, PREDATING both 0.9.24
# and 0.9.25, while mise ran 0.9.25 — so every "how does graphify work?" answer
# came from the wrong source, and several were wrong.
#
# Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch head:
#   - `ref = v8` (the old value) is a BRANCH — it drifts ahead of the release, so
#     the corpus would describe unreleased code.
#   - The newest tag is also wrong: `v1.0.0` is tagged on GitHub but is NOT on
#     PyPI (PyPI latest = 0.9.25, verified 2026-07-23), and mise installs from
#     PyPI — so tracking newest-tag would ingest code we cannot run.
# The correct ref is `v<version>` for the version uv resolves.
#
# ⚠️ FORKED 2026-08-24 (Ray). THE URL BELOW IS NO LONGER UPSTREAM, and the
# invariant above is why it had to move with the pin: `pyproject.toml` now
# installs `graphifyy[all]` from `git+https://github.com/ray-manaloto/graphify@
# cdfb11c0…`, so leaving this at Graphify-Labs would have put the corpus back in
# exactly the 2026-07-23 state described above — describing code we do not run —
# while every surface still LOOKED pinned.
#
# WHY THE FORK, as measured ON 2026-08-24: graphify 0.9.48 had no codex backend,
# and neither did upstream `v8` (byte-identical to v0.9.48 at that moment;
# control-armed — `compare/v0.9.47...v8` reported ahead_by 14, so the endpoint
# discriminates). Both halves are frozen to that date on purpose: `v8` has since
# moved to v0.9.49, so re-read it rather than quoting this. PR #2981 adds
# `openai-cli`, a
# sibling of `claude-cli` that shells to the locally authenticated `codex` CLI,
# and it is OPEN and unreviewed. Ray's call was to take the whole branch rather
# than cherry-pick, so this pins its head verbatim.
#
# THE REF IS A BRANCH WE CREATED, and that contradicts the "never a branch head"
# rule above for one specific reason: `refs/heads/kb-pin/openai-cli-backend-v0.9.49`
# (the ref recorded below — the branch is renamed per rebase base) in
# our fork exists ONLY to hold this commit. Nothing pushes to it, so it cannot
# drift the way `v8` does. The `commit` below is still the authority; the branch
# is there so the object survives if TelB-io (whose fork the PR head lives on)
# deletes their branch. Forks share object storage within a network, which is how
# a SHA authored on TelB-io/graphify is reachable here at all.
#
# ⚠️ THE VERSION STRING DOES NOT MOVE WITH THE FORK. It reported `0.9.48` when the
# fork was cut and reports `0.9.49` now — but only because UPSTREAM released; the
# fork's own seven commits changed nothing about it. Same name, same version as
# the release it sits on, different code. So version alone cannot tell a forked
# install from an upstream one, which is precisely why `currency.toml`
# `[tool.graphify]` needed a fork-aware state rather than a bumped number.
#
# THE INSTRUMENT THAT CAN TELL, found 2026-08-25: the installed distribution's own
# `direct_url.json` records the commit uv ACTUALLY installed —
#   uv run python -c "from importlib.metadata import distribution; \
#     print(distribution('graphifyy').read_text('direct_url.json'))"
# That is the runtime speaking, where every file below is only a claim about it.
#
# WHAT RETURNS THIS TO UPSTREAM: #2981 merging and shipping to PyPI. Then revert
# `pyproject.toml` to `graphifyy[all]==<that version>`, set url/ref/commit here
# back to `Graphify-Labs` at the matching tag, and drop the fork block in
# currency.toml. Upstream ships roughly daily (15 releases in 15 days measured
# 2026-08-24), so re-check rather than assume.
#
# To bump the FORK: rebase the `kb-pin/openai-cli-backend-<base>` branch onto the
# newer upstream tag, push, then set `commit` here and the `@<sha>` in
# `pyproject.toml` together. They are one pin in two files and must move in the
# same commit — and `currency.toml`'s `ref_binding` rows are what find the OTHER
# surfaces carrying the same SHA, which a research lane under-counted 3-to-7 once.
#
# ⚠️ THERE IS NO REBASE TARGET RIGHT NOW — re-measured 2026-08-25. Upstream's
# DEFAULT branch is `v8`, not `main` (`main` has been frozen at 91f4d120 since
# 2026-05-14, so reading it reports a three-month-old tree as "latest"). `v8` HEAD
# is 282976b2, which IS the `v0.9.49` tag; `compare/282976b2...cdfb11c0` on our
# fork reports ahead_by 7, behind_by 0. #2981 remains OPEN and `dirty`, its head
# 1d0a9338 untouched since 2026-08-24T10:09 — before this fork was cut, so there
# is nothing new on its side either. Re-measure before assuming this still holds.
url = https://github.com/ray-manaloto/graphify
ref = kb-pin/openai-cli-backend-v0.9.49
commit = cdfb11c000ccbe3af1fbd1b9c41ab42718d54fc8
kind = code
added = 2026-07-21
